WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.880
In today’s world, the results of scientific&nbsp;
research need to get out to the public domain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.160
as soon as possible, partly because academia has&nbsp;
become highly competitive and authors need to show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.360
their recent work for the purposes of funding, job&nbsp;
applications, and career progression in general.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.000
Besides, timely dissemination of research results&nbsp;
is required to accelerate scientific progress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.040
This is particularly important in some&nbsp;
fields such as biology and medicine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.760
where it can influence healthcare related&nbsp;
developments, decisions, and policies; and in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:44.000
computer science and information technology, where&nbsp;
the pace of scientific progress is very fast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.880
The need to share research findings immediately&nbsp;
and the growing frustration of scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.120
at the slow pace of academic journals has&nbsp;
led to the trend of distributing preprints.&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.320
What is a preprint?
A preprint is a completed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.880
draft of a scientific manuscript that is&nbsp;
uploaded by the author on a public server;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.480
often it is the same version of the&nbsp;
manuscript that is submitted to a journal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.480
Once the manuscript is uploaded, it goes through a&nbsp;
quick check to ascertain that it is scientific in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.560
nature. It is then posted online within a day&nbsp;
or two without peer review and is made freely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.640
available for everyone to view. Revised versions&nbsp;
of the same manuscript can be uploaded later on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.600
but the older versions also remain.
Popular preprints servers in different fields&nbsp;

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:36.720
There are several sites that host preprints,&nbsp;
often known as preprint servers or repositories.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.360
While some of the preprint severs&nbsp;
host papers from various disciplines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:47.360
others cater only to selected disciplines. The&nbsp;
oldest and most popular one is arXiv which was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:53.120
created back in the 1990s for distributing&nbsp;
physics preprints. The site currently hosts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.640
papers from various disciplines such as physics,&nbsp;
mathematics, computer science, and statistics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:06.400
The main players in the field of the life sciences&nbsp;
are bioRxiv and PeerJ PrePrints. Nature also has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:12.160
preprint server, Nature Precedings, for biology,&nbsp;
medicine, chemistry, and earth science papers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.080
Social science and humanities preprints can&nbsp;
be posted on Social Science Research Network.&nbsp;

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.040
Some of the benefits of publishing&nbsp;
a preprint may include :&nbsp;

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:30.720
No delays : The most obvious benefit of using&nbsp;
preprints is that it removes the element of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:36.640
delay in the journal publication process, and&nbsp;
others can benefit from your work immediately .
 &nbsp;

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:41.440
Open access : Depositing your work in&nbsp;
a preprint server is a great way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:45.040
make your research freely available&nbsp;
to all scientists across the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:52.560
This is also known as green open access .
 
Establish priority : At a time when many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.440
scientists across the world might be working on&nbsp;
the same research idea, putting up a preprint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:02.480
can help establish your priority on an idea or&nbsp;
discovery as preprint servers generally mention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:08.480
the date on which the article was posted .
 
Receive valuable feedback on your work :&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.880
Once you have posted a preprint, you can send&nbsp;
the link to fellow scientists asking for their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:20.080
feedback. Sometimes, scientists spot an error in&nbsp;
your paper and comment on it. You can use such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.560
feedback to judge the quality of your work and&nbsp;
improve it before you submit it to a journal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.600
This will increase its chances of&nbsp;
getting accepted by the journal .
 &nbsp;

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.640
Get early attention : Papers posted on&nbsp;
preprints servers are usually citable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:39.440
and thus, you stand a chance of being cited even&nbsp;
before your paper is published in a journal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.080
If scientists like your study, they&nbsp;
might even share it on social media.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.240
Thus, you can get attention for your research&nbsp;
even before it is officially published .
 &nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.360
Provide evidence of your research : Funding&nbsp;
agencies and hiring committees often want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:01.040
see evidence of your recent work. Thus, delays&nbsp;
in publishing can be extremely damaging when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:08.160
are applying for grants or for a job. Preprints&nbsp;
are extremely useful under such circumstances .
 &nbsp;

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:14.240
Increase chances of collaboration and invitations&nbsp;
to meetings : Conference and seminar organizers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:18.000
are often on the lookout for people to&nbsp;
present work that has not yet been published.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.960
A preprint increases your visibility&nbsp;
and can attract meeting organizers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.080
as well as potential collaborators .   
 
and, Gain visibility for a broad range&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.200
of findings : Novelty is often a prime&nbsp;
criterion for being published in a journal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:38.800
Thus, it can be difficult for authors to&nbsp;
publish null findings or replication studies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:45.640
Preprints eliminate this problem by providing&nbsp;
visibility to a much broader range of findings .&nbsp;

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.960
However , there are Some concerns about preprints.&nbsp;

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:58.320
The most important concern that the&nbsp;
scientific community has about preprints&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.840
is that they are not peer reviewed. Peer review&nbsp;
is an essential quality control mechanism to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:09.600
weed out essentially flawed or poor quality&nbsp;
studies. Additionally, without peer review,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.080
there is a possibility of incorrect information&nbsp;
reaching the general public through preprints.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:21.200
This can be potentially harmful in areas such&nbsp;
as climate science or vaccine safety. Thus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:26.960
some kinds of work may not be appropriate for&nbsp;
dissemination through preprints. Another possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:37.840
problem is that scientists might upload articles&nbsp;
or findings prematurely just to claim priority.

